; =============================================================================
; This code is very sloppy, being that it is a hacked-together disassembly
; meant for one assembler, converted to another, and then patched bit by bit.
;
; The core Microsoft Basic interpreter has had the bugfixes added up through
; version 2.3 (FPBASIC is 2.0).  See https://github.com/mist64/msbasic
;
; Some Apple-specific functionality was removed (dummied-out commands will
; raise an ADVANCED FEATURE error) and new functionality added:
;
;   * Upon cold start, the amount of free memory will be displayed
;     (as in most other Microsoft dialects).  Upon warm start, the message
;     "Ok" (again as in most other Microsoft dialects) is displayed.
;   * Some Apple commands have been replaced by ones more useful here: VDP,
;     VPOKE, VPEEK, ELSE, WPOKE, WPEEK and SWAP.  (Note that ELSE must be 
;     preceded by a colon.)
;   * Tokens are case-insensitive and will always be stored in the program as
;     uppercase, as on the Apple //c and later.
;   * $XX hexadecimal numeric constants are supported (the opposite, HEX$, is
;     not yet implemented).
;   * AND, OR, NOT and comparisons restored to the original behavior.
;   * HGR, HPLOT, HCOLOR=, TEXT are working, more or less; HPLOT TO does not
;     work (is not implemented).
;   * DEFSPR and DRAW to manipulate the sprite tables.
;
; Cosmetic bug: Variable names are not case-smashed until evaluated.
;
; In addition to &, SAVE and LOAD are now user-vectored ($03D0 resp. $03D3).
; By default, they will raise "Advanced Feature Error", but they can be wired
; to do anything.
;
; Source for ELSE and SWAP is Beagle Basic by Mark Simonson.
; Source for $XX, WPOKE and WPEEK is EHBASIC by Lee Davison.
;
; The space in the table currently occupied by PDL should be given to HEX$
; once it can be implemented.  Anything else pointed to L3ERR needs to be
; replaced with something else.
; =============================================================================

          .ORG      $C000

          JMP       COLD_START
          JMP       RESTART

;--------------------------------
;   ZERO PAGE LOCATIONS:
;--------------------------------
GOWARM          =  $00        ;GETS "JMP RESTART"
